well several youth from west las vegas  community were able to have in-depth  conversations with law enforcement today  in a know your rights workshop this  happened at doolittle community center 8  news now reporter victoria saha takes a  look at why these events help build  trust on both sides  the teams and law enforcement i spoke  with say events like this helps them  understand both perspectives if they  were to be approached by law enforcement  so there could be trust coming from both  sides close to 60 youth joined the  conversation at doolittle community  center to understand what to do when  approached by police  twelve-year-old jahi hodge was amongst  them i want to learn how to deactivate a  situation in that when i am with a  police officer as to not you know make  the wrong move or do the wrong action  officer adrian hunt grew up in the area  he says he sees himself in these  participants and wants them to know it's  okay to trust police when i do do the  workshops they say hey does anybody have  family or friends in law enforcement and  i tell them okay what you do now you  know and i give them my email contact  information so if they have any  questions or any you know if they feel  like they've been maybe in a situation  and they're not certain they can reach  out to somebody the event had  explanations of different scenarios and  showed the rights and responsibilities  that the community has when stopped by  police it makes them comfortable as well  and makes them see okay that i can  understand where he's coming from now  one mom joined her daughter in the  workshop she hopes these lessons stick  with her daughter hopefully that she is  aware to just stay calm  to know that she hasn't done anything  wrong and to make sure that she is  obeying what the officer is saying and  we can handle the rest at a later time  if she feels like she is being violated  or anything of that nature a key  takeaway from this event is to let youth  know if they were to encounter police  then they need to just stay calm and  comply running away is not the option in  the newsroom victoria zaha 8 news
 

